# Rule: SwiftUI Preferences System

Sources

https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/preferences

Core Principle

SwiftUI preferences are an upward communication channel.

Rules

- Use preferences only when information must move from descendants up to ancestors.
- Prefer environment for downward contextual data.
- Prefer bindings for editable downward data access.
- Use preferences primarily for layout, geometry, and container coordination.
- Keep preference keys narrow and semantically focused.
- Let ancestors interpret preferences; children should only emit them.

Anti-Patterns

- Preferences as an event bus.
- Business data ownership in preference values.
- Catch-all preference keys for unrelated concerns.
